# Parallel research team

Agents work like lab colleagues: **one workstream each**, shared frozen interfaces, no stepping on each other.

## Workstreams (pick exactly one per Task/subagent)
| Tag | Owns | Must not touch |
|---|---|---|
| `sim-scene` | In-repo Isaac scene, **Foresight** expert SM, collection | filter math, policy nets, DynamicVLA SM |
| `perception` | detector→tracker→Kalman, 3D lift | policy training, reflex |
| `policy` | SmolVLA/LeRobot conditioning + Δ/noise aug | sim PhysX knobs, executor |
| `control` | timestamped buffer, reflex, safety/coast | dataset schemas, training |
| `eval` | speed sweeps, RMSE, failure taxonomy, gates | production control loops |
| `explore` | read-only search / docs | any writes |

## Parallelism rules
1. Tag every Task prompt: `WORKSTREAM: <tag>`. Hooks enforce this for general-purpose subagents.
2. **Shared interface files** (`interfaces/`, state message schema) — change only with an explicit handoff note; prefer additive fields behind flags.
3. Prefer disjoint paths: `sim/`, `perception/`, `policy/`, `control/`, `eval/`.
4. Launch independent workstreams in **parallel** (multiple Task calls). Serialize only when they share a file or gate.
5. Subagent return format: **result / evidence / open questions** — no speculative roadmaps.

## Parent agent duties
- Assign workstreams, merge results, run gate checks.
- Never let two writers edit the same module concurrently.
- After merges: one sanity check (shapes/seeds/import) before scaling GPU jobs.

Full contract: `AGENTS.md`.
